    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello, \r\n\r\nI use mini.nvim files and picker to open files.\r\nI also use picker to list buffers.\r\n\r\nOften, fully-qualified paths are used, instead of relative paths. \r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/5642902/3299a615-56c8-493d-9b89-17603e602889)\r\n\r\nIs there a way to change this and use relative paths across these plugins?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I use mini.nvim files and picker to open files.<br>\nI also use picker to list buffers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Often, fully-qualified paths are used, instead of relative paths.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/347137338-3299a615-56c8-493d-9b89-17603e602889.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..yj2qE6e7tJR5PI0CDezhbNYel5MYSl056r3kTqpJ-VE\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/347137338-3299a615-56c8-493d-9b89-17603e602889.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..yj2qE6e7tJR5PI0CDezhbNYel5MYSl056r3kTqpJ-VE\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to change this and use relative paths across these plugins?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello,\nI use mini.nvim files and picker to open files.\nI also use picker to list buffers.\nOften, fully-qualified paths are used, instead of relative paths.\nFor example:\n\nIs there a way to change this and use relative paths across these plugins?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-07-10T07:56:30Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If you mean `:Pick files`, then its items are computed with [configured CLI tool](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1055-L1066) (`rg` by default) with possible fallback to a built-in \"fallback\" method. For me with `rg` it shows paths relative to current working directory (which you can see with `:pwd`).\r\n\r\nIf you mean `:Pick buffers`, then it uses the output of a `:buffers` command, which also tries to use relative paths.\r\n\r\nSo it already does what you're asking for. Maybe you have current working directory not the one you expect (check with `:pwd`)?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">If you mean <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick files</code>, then its items are computed with <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1055-L1066\">configured CLI tool</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> by default) with possible fallback to a built-in \"fallback\" method. For me with <code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> it shows paths relative to current working directory (which you can see with <code class=\"notranslate\">:pwd</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you mean <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick buffers</code>, then it uses the output of a <code class=\"notranslate\">:buffers</code> command, which also tries to use relative paths.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So it already does what you're asking for. Maybe you have current working directory not the one you expect (check with <code class=\"notranslate\">:pwd</code>)?</p>",
            "bodyText": "If you mean :Pick files, then its items are computed with configured CLI tool (rg by default) with possible fallback to a built-in \"fallback\" method. For me with rg it shows paths relative to current working directory (which you can see with :pwd).\nIf you mean :Pick buffers, then it uses the output of a :buffers command, which also tries to use relative paths.\nSo it already does what you're asking for. Maybe you have current working directory not the one you expect (check with :pwd)?",
